WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
Speaker 1: I don't want to spend a ton of time on&nbsp;
this because we're going to be covering it live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:08.320
tonight. But one of the things that is expected&nbsp;
to be shown tonight at what is as of now the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:14.720
last January six committee hearing are videos&nbsp;
of Trump trying to record that bizarre speech&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:21.440
to the rioters right after the January 6th riots.&nbsp;
And outtakes will be published tonight during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:27.600
hearing, which will show Donald Trump struggling&nbsp;
through his post riot speech. The report is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:35.040
Trump was visibly struggling with what to say, not&nbsp;
wanting to say certain things, clearly trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:42.400
deliver a recorded video about the riots that&nbsp;
would not make Trump look like he was happy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:48.240
about the violence, which it sort of seems&nbsp;
like he was, but also would not anger and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:55.920
isolate or alienate his supporters. And those are&nbsp;
expected to be shown tonight. Here's a little bit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:01.120
of a preview of that from last night on CNN.
Speaker 3: Jeffrey, the January six committee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.120
has snippets of outtakes from Trump's&nbsp;
taped message the day after the riot.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:08.960
Listen to what this is, what Congressman&nbsp;
Adam Schiff told me about it tonight. Watch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:17.440
There are people urging him to say things to try&nbsp;
to get the the rioters, the attackers to go home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:22.160
There are things that they that he&nbsp;
can't be prevailed upon to do and say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:28.960
not for hours and hours. And and then ultimately,&nbsp;
when he does give a statement. Still things he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:34.560
wouldn't say. And so you'll have to wait until&nbsp;
tomorrow evening to see precisely what that is.&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.040
Speaker 1: We are going to be covering&nbsp;
that live tonight on YouTube, Twitch and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.520
Facebook. I hope that you will join me. I&nbsp;
don't have more to say about it right now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.840
We'll let those snippets speak for themselves&nbsp;
tonight. Find me on Twitter at David Pakman.

